1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:36,286
<i>They're former assassins.</i>

2
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:37,537
Former Concordat members.

3
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:38,580
And according to Chiara,

4
00:00:38,663 --> 00:00:40,999
if anyone knows how they operate,
it's them!

5
00:00:41,082 --> 00:00:42,959
<i>La Morte Bianca and the Concordat.</i>

6
00:00:43,042 --> 00:00:45,086
That the Los Bandidos
could be a huge help.

7
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:47,756
I'm not saying I like the approach, but…

8
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:49,007
I get the logic.

9
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:09,694
Los Bandidos.

10
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,406
<i>I know how dangerous they are,</i>
<i>all of them.</i>

11
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:15,283
<i>I just don't want anyone getting hurt.</i>

12
00:01:15,366 --> 00:01:17,577
No one wants anyone to get hurt.

13
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:21,331
But you don't always
have to be the one taking action.

14
00:01:21,414 --> 00:01:22,791
Sometimes,

15
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:25,668
a team moves faster

16
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:27,295
than a lone hero.

17
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:33,259
- Discreetly?
- Who, sir?

18
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:56,241
Hey, look at you.

19
00:01:56,324 --> 00:01:58,743
Your face might get stuck like that.

20
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:00,245
Your forehead was all…

21
00:02:00,328 --> 00:02:01,496
See? Like that.

22
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:03,081
Mm.

23
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:08,169
I guess I miss them.

24
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:09,546
Your parents?

25
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:12,715
Yes, and Mikoy too.

26
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:15,009
He's such a goofball.

27
00:02:15,093 --> 00:02:17,220
When he's around,

28
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:18,596
it's so noisy.

29
00:02:19,472 --> 00:02:20,723
But when he's gone,

30
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:23,226
it's way too quiet.

31
00:02:24,811 --> 00:02:25,895
I don't know.

32
00:02:26,521 --> 00:02:27,438
And then,

33
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:29,649
so much is happening right now.

34
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:31,818
Meanwhile, I'm…

35
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:35,196
just here.

36
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,700
Feels like I'm not helping much.

37
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:41,411
Oh, Angelito.

38
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:43,830
Just because you're not there

39
00:02:43,913 --> 00:02:46,207
doesn't mean you're not helping, okay?

40
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:51,087
You know what they say.
Worry is a waste of imagination.

41
00:02:51,671 --> 00:02:54,090
But I also know

42
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:55,884
it's not easy to stop worrying.

43
00:02:56,384 --> 00:02:59,679
Especially when it's someone you love.

44
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:03,516
So I'm not going to stop you.

45
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:10,607
But if you can, just breathe.

46
00:03:11,107 --> 00:03:13,568
You might end up scaring me.

47
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:15,153
How?

48
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:17,447
How?

49
00:03:18,531 --> 00:03:21,618
You might scare me
because wrinkles won't suit you.

50
00:03:21,701 --> 00:03:22,577
See? Right there.

51
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:25,788
You're impossible.

52
00:03:25,872 --> 00:03:27,206
There you go!

53
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:32,003
You look much better smiling.
Your cute baby face really shows.

54
00:03:35,173 --> 00:03:36,341
But honestly…

55
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:38,801
I'm really scared.

56
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:43,431
So,

57
00:03:43,932 --> 00:03:45,683
I came up with a plan.

58
00:03:47,685 --> 00:03:48,770
You know…

59
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:51,814
Daddy Sir isn't
the only police officer I know.

60
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:54,275
Leave it to me.

61
00:03:57,612 --> 00:03:58,446
<i>Rafa?</i>

62
00:03:59,030 --> 00:03:59,989
I need a favor.

63
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:01,824
<i>It's just that…</i>

64
00:04:01,908 --> 00:04:03,868
For our community outreach report,

65
00:04:03,952 --> 00:04:06,371
we need some

66
00:04:06,454 --> 00:04:08,289
supplementary data.

67
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:11,876
The signal here is really slow.

68
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:14,420
Could you send it over?

69
00:04:14,504 --> 00:04:16,756
Sorry, Sofie. I can't help you
with that right now.

70
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:17,674
I'm really busy.

71
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:19,717
That busy?

72
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:23,054
Please print this.

73
00:04:23,137 --> 00:04:26,057
Forward this. Check this.

74
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:28,726
- And this too.
- <i>Ben!</i>

75
00:04:29,227 --> 00:04:30,311
<i>Ben, you’re not my boss.</i>

76
00:04:32,522 --> 00:04:34,983
I hope they find the chemical bomb soon.

77
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:40,613
The… Ben wants to watch their concert.

78
00:04:41,864 --> 00:04:42,865
What?

79
00:04:44,325 --> 00:04:45,451
Yes.

80
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:48,413
<i>My Chemical Romance.</i>

81
00:04:51,082 --> 00:04:52,625
Oh, right.

82
00:04:57,005 --> 00:05:00,216
Anyway, Sofie, I have to go.
Take care. Bye-bye.

83
00:05:02,552 --> 00:05:03,594
What are you doing?

84
00:05:04,721 --> 00:05:07,015
That's General Norberto's daughter.

85
00:05:08,891 --> 00:05:09,976
We're doomed.

86
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:13,938
What did he say? What's going on?

87
00:05:15,356 --> 00:05:17,817
Well… Nothing.

88
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:19,986
Nothing. There's…

89
00:05:20,069 --> 00:05:22,071
nothing going on. I think.

90
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:24,782
But… Maybe there is something.

91
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:26,367
I just don't know what.

92
00:05:28,786 --> 00:05:29,787
Anyway.

93
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:51,309
It's unfair, isn't it?

94
00:05:56,981 --> 00:05:59,233
It's so beautiful and peaceful here.

95
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:02,070
It's like the only thing
you have to worry about

96
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:03,696
is what you're having for dinner.

97
00:06:06,365 --> 00:06:08,701
Meanwhile, back home…

98
00:06:10,036 --> 00:06:11,370
everything is falling apart.

99
00:06:15,041 --> 00:06:16,542
Frustrating.

100
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:20,922
I should be used to this kind of life.

101
00:06:28,471 --> 00:06:29,931
I'm still from here.

102
00:06:30,014 --> 00:06:31,724
I still don't want

103
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:34,977
people dying because of this conflict.

104
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:46,447
I don’t know. It just…

105
00:06:48,116 --> 00:06:50,868
makes me want to go back to a simple life.

106
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:02,755
Honestly, we're already embarrassed.

107
00:07:02,839 --> 00:07:04,799
Gosh. Come on.

108
00:07:04,882 --> 00:07:06,717
You're our guests. Don't be embarrassed.

109
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:08,136
Oh, all right.

110
00:07:08,219 --> 00:07:09,053
If that's the case.

111
00:07:09,137 --> 00:07:12,432
It feels like we're the ones
being taken care of.

112
00:07:12,515 --> 00:07:14,058
That's all right.

113
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:16,769
That's how we treat our guests here.

114
00:07:16,853 --> 00:07:19,439
It's also our way of thanking you.

115
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:21,274
Because of your help,

116
00:07:21,357 --> 00:07:23,943
our community is becoming a better place.

117
00:07:24,026 --> 00:07:25,611
Just be careful.

118
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:28,322
Don't wander off to the other islands.

119
00:07:30,032 --> 00:07:31,159
Why?

120
00:07:31,242 --> 00:07:34,620
The neighboring island
was suddenly raided.

121
00:07:35,746 --> 00:07:36,622
Raided?

122
00:07:37,206 --> 00:07:39,125
We still don't know by whom.

123
00:07:39,208 --> 00:07:41,169
They said there were armed men

124
00:07:41,794 --> 00:07:43,296
looking for something.

125
00:07:43,379 --> 00:07:45,089
Some say it was a person.

126
00:07:45,673 --> 00:07:47,884
Others say it wasn't.

127
00:07:48,551 --> 00:07:49,552
Not a person?

128
00:07:50,136 --> 00:07:52,472
Who knows? Some say treasure.

129
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:56,142
Others say… a bomb.

130
00:08:01,230 --> 00:08:07,778
NORBERTO S. RUIZ
GENERAL

131
00:08:33,804 --> 00:08:36,432
Wait… Why does he look different
in these photos?

132
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:48,319
Me? No.

133
00:08:48,402 --> 00:08:50,029
- No.
- But…

134
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:05,211
Even his voice… It's like…

135
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:07,213
- Here we go.
- Oh.

136
00:09:08,089 --> 00:09:09,715
All right. You don't know me.

137
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:11,384
- I'm sorry.
- Please leave.

138
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:13,636
See? That's not him.

139
00:09:19,475 --> 00:09:21,269
<i>There are inconsistencies, sir.</i>

140
00:09:21,978 --> 00:09:24,272
They're minor, so they're
not that obvious, but…

141
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:44,333
So no investigation ever moved forward,
and there were no formal complaints.

142
00:09:47,211 --> 00:09:50,214
He's practically friends with everyone.

143
00:10:15,781 --> 00:10:17,742
What did I miss?

144
00:10:19,535 --> 00:10:23,080
What are you hiding, Senator Quintin?

145
00:10:32,882 --> 00:10:34,508
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

146
00:10:34,592 --> 00:10:36,469
We're playing charades today!

147
00:10:36,552 --> 00:10:38,262
Perfect. We have two teams.

148
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:40,681
This team is the fair-skinned team.

149
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:44,727
And this team has one fair-skinned
and one kinda fair-skinned.

150
00:10:45,311 --> 00:10:46,479
- Come on.
- Fighting.

151
00:10:47,063 --> 00:10:49,982
And of course,
today's category is animals!

152
00:10:50,066 --> 00:10:51,651
Hey, they said "animal"!

153
00:10:52,777 --> 00:10:54,028
There you go. Come over here.

154
00:10:54,111 --> 00:10:56,155
There! There!

155
00:10:56,238 --> 00:10:59,033
Whichever team loses

156
00:10:59,116 --> 00:11:02,036
- has to wash butts.
- Butts?

157
00:11:02,119 --> 00:11:03,162
Glasses!

158
00:11:03,829 --> 00:11:04,914
And plates as well!

159
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:06,707
Those are some high stakes!

160
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:08,334
- Yep! Are you ready?
- Ready!

161
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:10,294
All right, here's your category.

162
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:12,505
Do it properly!

163
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:13,923
Game on!

164
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:20,388
That's so easy!

165
00:11:20,971 --> 00:11:21,931
You've got this!

166
00:11:23,182 --> 00:11:24,809
Wrong! Shark!

167
00:11:26,143 --> 00:11:28,145
Time's up!

168
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:31,982
You still have zero points.
Who's guessing next?

169
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,192
Of course, the fairer one.

170
00:11:34,276 --> 00:11:36,404
Don't let them see it.
Here's your category.

171
00:11:36,487 --> 00:11:37,947
- Alex! Alex!
- There, Alex!

172
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:40,241
Who's guessing first?

173
00:11:40,324 --> 00:11:42,159
Go, Bok, go!

174
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:43,828
- Get ready.
- Go on.

175
00:11:43,911 --> 00:11:45,121
Do your best, Bok!

176
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:47,581
- You okay?
- There!

177
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:50,084
Do you want to join?

178
00:11:58,134 --> 00:11:58,968
That's a long one!

179
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:07,560
- Correct?
- Already said.

180
00:12:08,269 --> 00:12:09,812
- Hey!
- Oh, come on. Elephant!

181
00:12:13,566 --> 00:12:15,860
- Yay! Hooray!
- Amazing!

182
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:18,279
- You won!
- Miss Tess is so great!

183
00:12:18,362 --> 00:12:22,491
You'll be washing the glasses!

184
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:31,167
That's deep.

185
00:12:31,792 --> 00:12:34,044
As deep as the Pacific Ocean.

186
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:27,681
I would choose them.

187
00:13:33,687 --> 00:13:38,943
<i>Universe, please show me a sign</i>
<i>that everything will be okay eventually.</i>

188
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:48,410
Why are you here?

189
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:50,829
Can't sleep?

190
00:13:52,414 --> 00:13:55,292
No. I can't wake up, that's why I'm here.

191
00:13:55,376 --> 00:13:57,878
You're being a smart aleck already.

192
00:13:57,962 --> 00:13:59,964
Fine, I won't bother you. I'll just leave.

193
00:14:00,047 --> 00:14:03,133
No, no! Don't go.

194
00:14:03,217 --> 00:14:04,760
- You can't even take a joke.
- See?

195
00:14:05,344 --> 00:14:06,595
Yes, you're right.

196
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:08,639
I can't sleep.

197
00:14:10,558 --> 00:14:11,392
Why?

198
00:14:12,309 --> 00:14:14,562
Is something on your mind?

199
00:14:14,645 --> 00:14:16,814
Is something bothering you?
Is that why you can't sleep?

200
00:14:18,148 --> 00:14:21,151
I have this feeling
that something isn't right.

201
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:25,197
Is it because of what
the foster family told us?

202
00:14:26,365 --> 00:14:29,368
About the other island?
The one that got raided?

203
00:14:31,036 --> 00:14:32,037
Maybe.

204
00:14:37,293 --> 00:14:38,127
Come here.

205
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:41,171
Look at me.

206
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:45,759
Everything will be okay.

207
00:14:48,637 --> 00:14:50,598
As long as we're together,

208
00:14:51,682 --> 00:14:53,309
nothing bad will happen.

209
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:55,853
So get some rest,

210
00:14:58,939 --> 00:15:02,192
I am not used to seeing
Sofie without a smile.

211
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:07,907
What did you call me? Ms. Overthinker?

212
00:15:07,990 --> 00:15:10,910
So you're saying I have two personalities?

213
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:13,495
Yes. Not just two.

214
00:15:13,579 --> 00:15:15,623
When the universe started
handing out moods,

215
00:15:15,706 --> 00:15:16,874
I think you caught them all.

216
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:18,542
You probably thought
they were all for you.

217
00:15:19,209 --> 00:15:20,878
Oh, is that so?

218
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:23,255
Go away, Mr. Checkered.

219
00:15:25,341 --> 00:15:26,508
Fine, I'll go.

220
00:15:28,552 --> 00:15:30,596
Okay, okay. I'm leaving.

221
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:34,308
Just kidding. Let's stay here
and feed the mosquitoes.

222
00:15:35,643 --> 00:15:38,354
Feed the mosquitoes? I'm used to them.

223
00:15:38,896 --> 00:15:40,022
- Used to them?
- Yes.

224
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:42,566
Stop pretending. You act like
you're used to them, but you're not.

225
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:58,207
Alex.

226
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:10,552
Cocoy left the safehouse.

227
00:16:11,595 --> 00:16:13,472
He took an international route,

228
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:15,641
and we only found out afterward.

229
00:16:52,845 --> 00:16:56,682
I'm not used to
operating with other people.

230
00:16:58,809 --> 00:16:59,977
I'm used to working alone.

231
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:31,902
Los Bandidos!

232
00:18:33,821 --> 00:18:35,405
La Fornarina!

233
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:45,624
It's strong!

234
00:19:10,232 --> 00:19:11,567
Stop.

235
00:19:13,735 --> 00:19:14,570
Why?

236
00:19:16,321 --> 00:19:18,949
You earned it. What do you want?

237
00:19:19,032 --> 00:19:20,450
Bertong Butete?

238
00:19:28,083 --> 00:19:29,042
Mario.

239
00:19:31,253 --> 00:19:34,006
Thank you for accepting this favor.

240
00:19:36,175 --> 00:19:37,759
This won't be easy.

241
00:19:43,223 --> 00:19:46,643
I understand. Of course, he's your friend.

242
00:19:47,895 --> 00:19:49,521
We still don't have solid evidence.

243
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:53,150
There's still no basis to take action.

244
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:57,446
And of course, I can't just ignore this.

245
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:59,072
<i>What about you?</i>

246
00:20:04,244 --> 00:20:05,412
Don't you want to look into it?

247
00:20:05,495 --> 00:20:09,041
Back when we were partners,
you were the one who always noticed

248
00:20:09,124 --> 00:20:11,460
the things I overlooked.

249
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:14,504
So I was the rebel,

250
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:16,673
and you were Mr. Memo.

251
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:20,636
You're also the one who quickly notices
when something's

252
00:20:20,719 --> 00:20:21,845
not right.

253
00:20:22,346 --> 00:20:26,850
I don't think I can
be objective about this.

254
00:20:28,018 --> 00:20:29,519
<i>He's my friend.</i>

255
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:30,896
Sometimes,

256
00:20:32,564 --> 00:20:34,816
you don't see people clearly

257
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:37,277
when you've trusted them for so long.

258
00:20:37,361 --> 00:20:39,238
So you want me to look into it?

259
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:43,909
I just have something more urgent
to focus on, Mario.

260
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:48,497
You know, Norberto, back then,
I used to get mad at you.

261
00:20:49,206 --> 00:20:50,707
Because I felt that

262
00:20:51,208 --> 00:20:52,918
while you were processing things,

263
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:56,129
the problems kept moving and piling up.

264
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:58,882
<i>But as time went on, I realized…</i>

265
00:20:59,758 --> 00:21:00,926
You were right.

266
00:21:01,009 --> 00:21:03,679
Someone really does need
to keep an eye on the bigger picture.

267
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:06,431
So people like us

268
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:08,308
can watch the flanks.

269
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:10,811
Thank you, then.

270
00:21:11,311 --> 00:21:12,938
Wait. Hold on.

271
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:15,190
There's a condition.

272
00:21:16,149 --> 00:21:19,361
What condition? Just name it, Mario.

273
00:21:21,196 --> 00:21:23,699
Never let anything happen to my family.

274
00:21:25,242 --> 00:21:26,326
Of course.

275
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:29,663
No matter what happens, promise me.

276
00:21:30,956 --> 00:21:32,499
I promise.

277
00:21:34,793 --> 00:21:35,711
Thank you.

278
00:21:37,504 --> 00:21:38,714
Thank you too.

279
00:21:41,341 --> 00:21:43,135
Take care, Mario.

280
00:21:50,976 --> 00:21:51,977
Was it Dad?

281
00:21:57,607 --> 00:21:59,943
I gave your father a mission.

282
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:04,114
So you're the one who sent him?

283
00:22:05,532 --> 00:22:07,534
We thought he ran away.

284
00:22:08,618 --> 00:22:09,619
You're right.

285
00:22:14,875 --> 00:22:17,127
Well, sir…

286
00:22:17,210 --> 00:22:19,421
I guess we're even now.

287
00:22:20,047 --> 00:22:22,132
Chiara and I ran away once, and then…

288
00:22:23,425 --> 00:22:26,136
it turns out you sent my dad on a mission.

289
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:29,556
Thank you for understanding, Mikoy.

290
00:22:31,308 --> 00:22:33,268
But don't tell anyone yet,
not even your mother.

291
00:22:33,351 --> 00:22:34,853
She'll only worry.

292
00:22:35,854 --> 00:22:37,647
You can count on me, sir.

293
00:22:37,731 --> 00:22:40,484
And I'm okay with that.

294
00:22:40,567 --> 00:22:44,279
I trust that you won't
let anything happen to Dad.

295
00:22:45,572 --> 00:22:47,949
I know that sometimes

296
00:22:48,033 --> 00:22:50,577
Chiara disobeys orders,
and you end up following her.

297
00:22:51,161 --> 00:22:53,205
But I understand you.

298
00:22:54,706 --> 00:22:59,252
What we're facing is just too big,
too difficult, and too dangerous.

299
00:22:59,336 --> 00:23:01,338
That's the problem we're up against.

300
00:23:04,216 --> 00:23:06,343
So maybe sometimes,

301
00:23:07,260 --> 00:23:10,972
we should maximize our differences.

302
00:23:13,058 --> 00:23:15,185
It's like… an all-star team, sir.

303
00:23:15,268 --> 00:23:17,813
Like joining forces.

304
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:19,022
Exactly!

305
00:23:20,065 --> 00:23:21,191
And I hope…

306
00:23:22,859 --> 00:23:24,694
we all succeed.

307
00:23:25,278 --> 00:23:26,571
Of course, sir.

308
00:23:27,072 --> 00:23:30,283
In the end, good will always prevail.

309
00:23:40,210 --> 00:23:44,673
My suggestions, meaning
you can either follow it or not.

310
00:23:48,176 --> 00:23:49,553
What’s your suggestion?

311
00:23:49,636 --> 00:23:53,974
Be ready for the time
you plan to finish her.

312
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:57,227
<i>I don’t bring</i>
<i>my personal feelings to work.</i>

313
00:23:57,310 --> 00:24:01,398
So whatever I said to you,
it’s purely because of work.

314
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:06,403
I can’t find Angelito.
Do you know where he is?

315
00:24:09,906 --> 00:24:11,908
<i>I might already been taking your time.</i>

316
00:24:11,992 --> 00:24:14,411
We’re here to help you out.

317
00:24:14,494 --> 00:24:15,287
RADIOACTIVE

318
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:21,585
It’s true, Alex.

319
00:24:28,967 --> 00:24:32,929
According to our Singaporean connections,
Cocoy is not there anymore.

320
00:24:33,013 --> 00:24:34,723
They’re already here in the Philippines.

321
00:24:34,806 --> 00:24:35,765
They?

322
00:24:35,849 --> 00:24:38,226
So it means the Los Bandidos are here?

323
00:24:38,310 --> 00:24:39,352
It looks like they are.
